    "summary": "I built a compact three-base desk unit with one drawer and a mount spike carrying a small platform. Its three bases sit in a triangle: two full bases at (0,0) and (1,0) and a north half base at (0,1). The drawer sits on the cut face of the half base. At the corner where all three bases meet there's a mount spike facing up, fitted with the small platform. A plain spike can't carry a platform, so it had to be the mount kind. I closed the open faces with 9 end caps and bolted the joints with 3 joint bolts. The build is 18 parts, about 1264 g of filament. The final check found no rule issues and no parts colliding. I didn't add any desk props, since you only asked for the parts.",
